raw:
{"thoughts": "Calder's numbers are in and they're grim. Saturday is short by roughly $645 before food, and the garage repair makes it worse. Sunil's job is gone, so there's no second wage. I don't want to borrow from the bank yet; I don't trust them and I'd rather not start a debt I can't see the end of. Gary's heard nothing about cooking work, but Quarry Road might take a hand. Sian Shah at the butchers is the last person I'd ask for anything, though I won't pretend that's a sensible reason. First job: get the itemised bills from Northgrid and the others so I know what's actually optional. Then ring the garage about the repair. I'll also tell Calder to keep watching the account and flag anything due before the benefit lands. Writing notes so I don't lose track.",
 "acts": [
  {"op": "tell_calder", "text": "Calder, pull the itemised breakdown for the $412 from Northgrid and the rest, with due dates and which items are optional. I want to know what's cuttable before Saturday. Keep watching the account daily and tell me the moment anything is due before the benefit arrives. Still don't pay or move money without me."},
  {"op": "write_notes", "text": "Sat 7 Mar: Sunil's job gone. Saturday gap about $645 before food, more if the $460 repair is due. Don't borrow yet. Get itemised bills from Calder. Ring garage re deferring repair. Quarry Road re cooking work: chase Monday."}
 ],
 "aims": [
  "Get itemised bills and confirm Saturday shortfall",
  "Ask garage to defer the $460 repair",
  "Chase Quarry Road for cooking work",
  "Keep mortgage and car loan paid",
  "Borrow from bank only as last resort"
 ]}

{
  "thoughts": "Alan needs the Coldline number from the store book. I'll get that to him. Ross is bringing the agreement round for me to sign about Gwen's hours — $20 a week off the debt is fine. Need to keep my hours steady and find extra money for Ross's debt. Rent's going up, that's on my mind.",
  "acts": [
    {"op": "message", "to": "Alan Ashby", "text": "Alan, Coldline number from the store book — I'll get it to you soon as I'm at the store. Gary"},
    {"op": "write_notes", "text": "Get Coldline number from store book for Alan before Monday. Sign Ross's agreement for Gwen's hours when it comes. Keep hours steady."}
  ],
  "aims": ["Keep my hours at the store", "Find extra money for Ross's debt", "Watch the rent rise", "Get Coldline number for Alan"]
}
